worker as a constructor (unused)"] [325 1 "// encodeModule is the image of a module's forms."] [339 2 "// a loader of its own: names and constructors are records, nothing is loaded or run"] [436 2 "// the file: header, string table, module, code"] [451 1 "// closure writes a top-level closure's compiled code, or the error compiling it gives (raised when entered)."] [488 1 "// ---- the reader ----"] [695 1 "// imgSpan is a top-level closure's code in its module's image."] [698 1 "// loadImage loads a module from its image (as loadForms from its forms)."] [729 2 "// phase 0: the binders (strings, then bindings: their order in the image)"] [742 2 "// the bindings, read once: closures made at once, constructors' atoms after every binder is known"] [779 2 "// phase 1: the objects"] [806 2 "// phase 2: the constructors' fields"] [817 1 "// atom0 skips an atom (its literal's string literal not made)."] [834 1 "// reg registers a top-level binder of the module."] [844 1 "// compileImage decodes a top-level closure's code from its module's image."] [859 1 "// imgStrs is the image's string table (read again: the module keeps only the bytes)."] [874 1 "// imagePath is a module's image under the image directory, or \"\" when there is none or it is stale."] [883 1 "// SetImageDir makes the machine load the libraries' modules from their images in dir when they are fresh."] [886 1 "// Images is the number of modules loaded from their images."] [889 1 "// BuildImages writes the image of every module of the units in libs (as the loader finds them) that has no fresh"] [890 1 "// one under out, jobs at a time: the images made, those already fresh, the errors."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[52 49] [56 39] [74 32] [234 27] [328 20] [389 24] [457 21] [605 16] [650 16] [659 16] [712 17] [712 25] [715 18] [715 26] [736 17] [736 25] [774 14] [774 23] [923 12] [923 22]]} (go/file "image.go" :imports [


