;; The binary image of the loaded code (HES32 (a), HE4d): a library module's STG compiled once into hsi's code
;; trees and written as bytes, one file a module (IMAGE/UNIT/MODULE.img), so a run decodes what it needs instead of
;; reading and compiling the forms. The format follows the loader's phases:
;;
;;	magic "hsimg" VERSION, the dump's size and modification time (the image is stale when either differs),
;;	the string table (every name and literal's bytes once), then the module: its data declarations (type
;;	constructors and their constructors' tags, arities and strictness), its string literals, its top-level
;;	bindings (a closure's update flag, arity and the span of its compiled code; a constructor's name and atoms),
;;	then the code: each top-level closure's compiled body (free variables, arguments and slots, the node tree,
;;	join points numbered within it), decoded when the closure is first entered.
;;
;; The bytes hold no pointers, so the collector does not scan them; only the code a run enters becomes nodes.
;; Integers are varints (zigzag for signed ones), floats their IEEE bits; a string literal and a label keep their
;; bytes and names (their addresses are a run's); a closure GHC's forms leave uncompilable keeps its error, raised
;; when it is entered, as the lazy compiler raises it.

